            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "droppedEvents": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 0
          },
          "refusedRows": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 0
          },
          "deliveredRows": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 0
          },
          "lastRefusalReason": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "fresh": {
            "type": "boolean"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "collector",
          "totalRuns",
          "lastRunAt",
          "lastSuccessAt",
          "consecutiveFailures",
          "circuitOpen",
          "droppedEvents",
          "refusedRows",
          "deliveredRows",
          "lastRefusalReason",
          "fresh"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "description": "Per-collector delivery and refusal counts, read from `collector_health` by `composition_root._collector_delivery_rows`. ABSENT means the health table could not be read at all; an empty list means every registered collector was read and none is registered — two different statements, which is why the section is optional rather than defaulted. `refusedRows` is the cumulative count of rows the source offered that were refused by named rule (ERR-256), and `lastRefusalReason` names the most frequent one plus the first place it happened; `droppedEvents` stays separate because it means events dropped from the collector's bounded queue, a different fault with a different remedy. `circuitOpen` is a boolean on purpose: the stored `circuit_open_until` is a `time.monotonic()` value from another process and means nothing to a reader. `fresh` is the SAME predicate `coverage.numerator` is counted with, so a collector cannot look healthy in one lane and stale in another."
    }
